# dropshadow

- Label: Drop Shadow
- Category: Copernicus (`Cop`), Houdini 22.0.368
- Inputs: 0 to 2
- Parameters: 38 (exact, read from Houdini by hython)
- Used by the height graph: no

## Feature summary (web, SideFX reference)

- Source: https://www.sidefx.com/docs/houdini/nodes/cop/dropshadow.html
- Summary (EN): Offsets a copy of the input layer, which can be expanded, streaked and blurred, then composites that shadow beneath the original. Listed as available since Houdini 22.0.
- Résumé (FR) : Crée une ombre portée à partir d'une copie décalée de la couche, étirable et floutée, placée sous l'original.

- Inputs meaning: ["source: original layer receiving the drop shadow", "mask: optional per-pixel mask scaled by the Mask parameter"]

- Key parameters: ["Mask: mix of new value with original; default 1", "Units: Image or Pixels for Offset, Distance, Expansion and Blur", "Output Drop Shadow Only: outputs only the shadow, for a separate AOV or later compositing", "Mode: Offset (X/Y vector) or Angle and Distance", "Color: shadow colour", "Multiply with Original: multiplies shadow colour with the original; when off the shadow colour replaces it", "Expansion and Maximum Radius: grow or shrink the shadow, with the maximum capping it", "Streak and Streak Weight: smear copies along the offset direction", "Blurring: Filter (Box or Gaussian, default Gaussian) and Scale Size per axis"]

- Caveats: ["Large Expansion values slow performance; Maximum Radius limits the cost.", "With Output Drop Shadow Only on, a Blend COP is needed to put the shadow back over the original.", "For text shadows or one-directional blur shadows the page points to the Font and Streak Blur nodes."]

